{"term":"haunt","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:de4ce76af0ef1dc6b0","definition":"To inhabit or to visit frequently (most often used in reference to ghosts).","example":"A couple of ghosts haunt the old, burnt-down house.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["dwell"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["come back to haunt","de-haunt","dehaunt","dishaunt","hauntable","hauntee","haunter","hauntology","hauntsome","haunty"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haunt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:04f8edfb1e5f53ea3e","definition":"To make uneasy, restless.","example":"The memory of his past failures haunted him.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["nag"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["come back to haunt","de-haunt","dehaunt","dishaunt","hauntable","hauntee","haunter","hauntology","hauntsome","haunty"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haunt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0ed757d0a18f47587c","definition":"To stalk; to follow.","example":"The policeman haunted him, following him everywhere.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["dwell"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["come back to haunt","de-haunt","dehaunt","dishaunt","hauntable","hauntee","haunter","hauntology","hauntsome","haunty"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haunt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:542f8a6ea2eb3a5da9","definition":"To live habitually; to stay, to remain.","example":"Ieſus therfore walked no more openly amõge the iewes : butt went his waye thence vnto a countre ny to a wildernes into a cite called effraym / and there haunted with his diſciples."